                        "review": "On the deck it starts with just a black screen.  On my Vivobook, it won't start period, just in limbo.\n\n\nTo Dev: I haven't done anything unusual with the steam deck, just some cache and temp file deletions here and there.  Mine doesn't use solid state, it's the one with the smaller longer lasting led one.  In case your running something different.  I was suprised because it uses a similar engine to Slave master which works on everything steam does.",
                        "timestamp_created": 1787937250,
                        "timestamp_updated": 1788033747,
                        "voted_up": false,
                        "votes_up": 1,
                        "votes_funny": 1,
                        "weighted_vote_score": 0.5222930312156677,
                        "comment_count": 0,
                        "steam_purchase": true,
                        "received_for_free": false,
                        "written_during_early_access": false,
                        "developer_response": "Hey,\n\nSo Valve did testing and determined that the game runs fine on the steam deck. I also have a steam deck that I purchased myself and I made sure all of my games run on it. They all use the exact same backend framework so it was pretty much just making sure the different controls are set up correctly.\n\nIs there anything specific that you had tried for that you did that may have caused this? Because I literally was play testing it on the steam deck less than a week ago. I can test it again on Monday when I am back and at my workstation.\n\nI haven't done any changes to the game that would cause it not to work so I'm not really sure why you are experiencing this.",
